## Add

**This project is a component of the [mulle-core](//github.com/mulle-core/mulle-core) library. As such you usually will *not* add or install it individually, unless you specifically do not want to link against `mulle-core`.**


{% 
   identifier = [[project.name uppercaseString] stringByReplacingOccurrencesOfString:@"-" withString:@"__"];
   tag        = [identifier stringByAppendingString:@"_TAG"];
   tagref     = [@"${" stringByAppendingString:tag];
   tagref     = [tagref stringByAppendingString:@"}"];
%}
### Add as a cmake subproject

{{ project.name }} is intended to be consumed as a cmake subproject with
[FetchContent](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/module/FetchContent.html) —
no mulle tooling is required in the parent build:

``` cmake
include( FetchContent)

set( {{ identifier }}_TAG "master" CACHE STRING "branch or tag to fetch {{ project.name }} from")

FetchContent_Declare( {{ identifier }}
   GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/{{ project.user }}/{{ project.name }}.git
   GIT_TAG        "{{ tagref }}")
FetchContent_MakeAvailable( {{ identifier }})

target_link_libraries( my_target PRIVATE {{ project.name }})
```

``` c
#include <{{ project.name }}/{{ project.name }}.h>
```

The parent project must supply the mulle dependency graph — `mulle-aba` and its transitive targets (e.g. by also adding `mulle-core`) — so that the dependency resolves to CMake targets rather than system libraries.


### Add with mulle-sde (mulle ecosystem)

Use [mulle-sde](//github.com/mulle-sde) to add {{ project.name }} to your project:

``` sh
mulle-sde add github:{{ project.user }}/{{ project.name }}
```


### Embed with clib (sources only)

To only add the sources of {{ project.name }} with dependency sources use [clib](https://github.com/clibs/clib):

``` sh
clib install --out src/{{ project.name }} {{ project.user }}/{{ project.name }}
```

Add `-isystem src/{{ project.name }}` to your `CFLAGS` and compile all the sources that were downloaded with your project.
